### LINK 1

**URL:** https://www.contentstack.com/docs/headless-cms/live-preview-implementation-for-nextjs-csr-app-router
**Posted by:** Chenowa George, 2026-07-09
**Classification:** Vendor documentation — RELEVANT
**Document scope:** Targets Next.js CSR (client-side rendering) with App Router, using Contentstack's REST Delivery SDK and the `@contentstack/live-preview-utils` SDK. Last updated July 22, 2026.

#### What the document says (quoted):

**Prerequisites — this is NOT configuration-only; code changes are required:**
> "Website that uses Contentstack Delivery SDKs"
> "Install and Initialize the Live Preview Utils SDK"

The document requires installing an npm package and writing initialization code:
> "npm install @contentstack/live-preview-utils@contentstack/utils"

SDK initialization (code, not config):
```js
ContentstackLivePreview.init({
  stackSdk: Stack,
  enable: true,
  ssr: false,
  editButton: { enable: true },
  stackDetails: {
    apiKey: "your api key",
    environment: "your environment value",
    branch: "your branch",
  },
  clientUrlParams: {
    protocol: "https",
    host: "app.contentstack.com",
    port: 443,
  },
});
```

**The `onEntryChange()` callback DOES take an argument** — it receives a function:
> "When you update an entry, the `onEntryChange()` method detects the change and runs your defined logic to fetch updated data."

```js
React.useEffect(() => {
  onEntryChange(updateData);
}, []);
```

**Configuration in Contentstack UI is also required (Settings > Environments + Visual Experience):**
> "Navigate to Settings and select Environments. Set the base URLs for different locales, and click Update."
> "Select Visual Experience from the stack settings. In the General tab, select the Enable Live Preview checkbox. Set the Default Preview Environment and click Save to save the settings."

**Live Preview icon appears at the entry level (not only the Visual Experience tab):**
> "You can now see the Live Preview icon within all the entries of your stack and the feature previews data from the hosted website."

**Live Edit tags are optional ("recommended"):**
> "Live Edit tags allow editors to directly jump from the Live Preview pane to the corresponding content fields in the entry editor."

#### Contradictions with story assumptions:

1. **"No code changes needed" assumption (V-NandaKumar KR: "Its possible, no code changes are needed and its more of configure and use")** — CONTRADICTED. The document requires installing an SDK package, writing initialization code, and wiring `onEntryChange()` into every page component that should support live preview. This is both code AND configuration.

2. **"Won't work from the Content type level" assumption (V-EPAM-Ivan Mikhailov: "It wont work from the Content type level (there is a 'Live preview' CTA). Its a CS bug (TBD)")** — The document states the Live Preview icon appears "within all the entries of your stack," suggesting it is designed to work at the entry/content-type level. If it does not, that would indeed be a bug, consistent with the ticket's TBD note.

3. **CSR-specific scope warning:** The document explicitly targets CSR with `ssr: false`. If the codeline uses SSR or a hybrid rendering model, this guide's initialization would need adaptation. The document title and `ssr: false` flag confirm this is the CSR variant only.

