### LINK 2

**URL:** https://www.contentstack.com/docs/headless-cms/custom-preview-urls#configure-custom-preview-urls
**Posted by:** V-EPAM-Ivan Mikhailov, 2026-07-27
**Classification:** Vendor documentation — RELEVANT (secondary)
**Document scope:** Describes Custom Preview URL configuration for Live Preview and Visual Editor. This is about URL pattern resolution for preview, not about the core Live Preview SDK setup. Last updated July 22, 2026.

#### What the document says (quoted):

**Custom Preview URLs are configured in the Contentstack UI, not in code:**
> "Go to your stack and click 'Settings'. Navigate to Visual Experience and select the Preview URL tab. Enable the Custom Preview URL toggle."

**Previous (default) behavior used a fixed pattern:**
> "Previously, Live Preview used a fixed pattern: `<environment base URL> + <entry's native URL field>`"

**Custom Preview URLs support dynamic patterns with placeholders:**
> "Placeholders use the `{{...}}` syntax and can reference: Entry fields: `{{entry.slug}}`, `{{entry.title}}`, `{{entry.uid}}`; Context variables: `{{environment}}, {{locale}}, {{branch}}, {{contentTypeUid}}`"

**Visual Editor cannot identify entries from custom URLs alone — additional code setup needed for Visual Editor:**
> "As a result, Visual Editor cannot identify the entry from the target URL alone. To open the correct entry, the Start editing button passes the entry UID and content type UID as page context. Configure this context once in your front-end code. For setup steps, refer to `setPageContext(context)` in the Live Preview Utils SDK config reference."

**Internal navigation requires no extra setup:**
> "For internal navigation, such as opening an entry from the entry list or the Tasks page, no extra setup is required, because Contentstack already passes the entry UID and content type UID in the URL."

**Plan availability note:**
> "Custom Preview URLs is available on select plans. Contact Contentstack support for more information."

#### Relevance to story:
This document addresses the ticket's concern about whether links/navigation works inside Live Preview. It confirms that Custom Preview URLs can handle nested routing, taxonomy-driven URLs, and multiple domains — but the default behavior is a simple `<base URL> + <URL field>` pattern. If the sites use complex routing (likely for GO/UP/MX), Custom Preview URL configuration would be needed. This is primarily a configuration task in the Contentstack UI, with a small code addition (`setPageContext`) only if using the Visual Editor mode.

